\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 How to Consult the Mo\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 Begin by Settling the Mind\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 Before consulting the Mo, pause.\
Let the mind become a little quieter. Let the urgency of the question soften just enough that you can hold it clearly. You do not need a perfectly blank mind, but you do need a sincere one.\
In the traditional method, one first visualizes Manjushri in the sky before oneself, then recites a prayer asking that what should be accepted and what should be discarded be made clear. After that, one recites the mantra of Manjushri and the mantra of interdependent origination, then casts while holding the question in mind. \
This sequence matters. It reminds us that the point is not to demand an answer, but to prepare the mind to receive one.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 The Role of the Mantra\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 A mantra is often described as 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec3 \'93that which protects the mind.\'94
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3  In this practice, the mantra is not an ornament and not merely a sacred phrase to set the mood. It is part of the method itself.\
The mantra of Manjushri is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec3 OM AH RA PA TSA NA DHI
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
In the traditional text, this is given as one of the principal mantras of Manjushri. The five middle syllables are said to represent the five Buddha families, while the final syllable, 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec3 DHI
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 , represents the wisdom of all the Buddhas. \
For practice, it is enough to understand this: the mantra is nothing less than 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec3 Manjushri himself in the form of sound
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 . To recite it is to orient the mind toward wisdom, clarity, and the cutting through of confusion. It protects the mind by gathering it, steadying it, and turning it away from fear, agitation, and scattered thought.\
When you recite or contemplate the mantra before a cast, you are not trying to \'93make the app work.\'94 You are entering the ritual properly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 Set the Intention Before the Cast\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 The cast should come after the question has already become clear in your mind.\
Do not cast first and search for a question afterward. Do not hold several different questions at once. Do not ask in a mood of panic, resentment, or restless repetition. The more confused the question, the harder it will be to understand the answer.\
A good approach is:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 settle the mind\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 bring one situation to mind\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 feel what is genuinely being asked\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 phrase it inwardly in a simple, direct way\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 then cast\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 In the traditional system, the answers are organized around concrete domains of life: family and livelihood, intentions and aims, friends and wealth, illness, spiritual practice, whether someone will come, whether a task will be accomplished, and all remaining matters. The system is practical. It works best when the question is practical too. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 What Makes a Question Good?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 A good question is:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 clear
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 singular
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 situated in real life
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 open to guidance
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 phrased so the answer can actually be used
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 A weak question is vague, sprawling, emotionally loaded, or impossible to interpret in action.\
The Mo is especially well suited to questions like:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 the direction of a relationship\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether a plan is favorable\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 how a difficulty is likely to unfold\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether support or resources are likely to gather\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether it is wise to proceed, wait, or reconsider\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 how to understand the conditions around illness, obstacles, or practice\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Because the entries speak in domains such as aspirations, relationships, wealth, health, and spiritual practice, the question should be formed in a way that allows those domains to answer it meaningfully. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 How to Phrase the Question\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 The best questions are usually simple and inwardly phrased, such as:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What are the conditions around this relationship?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Is it favorable to proceed with this plan?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 How is this undertaking likely to unfold?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What should I understand about this obstacle?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What are the conditions around my health in this matter?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Is this the right time to move forward?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What is the outlook for this aspiration?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 How should I understand this situation in my spiritual practice?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 These work well because they allow the result to speak in terms of support, obstruction, ripening, caution, strength, depletion, healing, timing, and alignment.\
Questions are usually less helpful when phrased as:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Will I definitely get exactly what I want?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Does this person secretly love me?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Will everything turn out perfectly?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What is going to happen to my whole life?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 These are either too absolute, too speculative, or too broad. They leave little room for interpretation and often invite wishfulness rather than clarity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 Ask One Question at a Time\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 If several concerns are entangled, choose the one that most needs light.\
Not:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Should I move, leave my relationship, change jobs, and start a new practice?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 But rather:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Is it favorable to make this move now?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What are the conditions around this relationship now?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 What is the outlook for this work decision?
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 One clear question leads to one interpretable answer.\
If the matter is very serious, the traditional text says it is good to make several predictions about it, including looking into it from different perspectives or for different times. If it is a small matter, one prediction is enough. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 Ask About Conditions, Not Control\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 The Mo is best consulted to understand 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec3 conditions
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec3 , not to seize certainty.\
Rather than forcing the future into a yes-or-no demand, ask in a way that allows wisdom to show:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether the path is open or obstructed\
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether support is present or lacking\
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether the matter is ripening or declining\
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 whether caution, patience, or confidence is called for\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 This is why many of the results make the most sense when the question has to do with outlook, alignment, timing, health, prosperity, spiritual obstacles, or the strength of an undertaking. The answer is often not a rigid verdict. It is a reading of the conditions. That is what makes it useful.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 Receive the Answer Properly\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 After the cast, do not rush to bend the answer to your preference.\
Read it slowly. Let the main tone register first. Notice what it says about strength or weakness, support or depletion, harmony or conflict, health or imbalance, prosperity or erosion, clarity or confusion. Then notice which part of your question it seems to illuminate most directly.\
Sometimes the answer confirms what you already sensed. Sometimes it reframes the situation. Sometimes it does not flatter your hopes. All of this is part of the practice.\
The purpose is not to be soothed at all costs. The purpose is to see more clearly what should be accepted and what should be discarded. That is the very prayer given at the beginning of the traditional method.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec3 A Final Word on Confidence\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec3 The usefulness of the Mo depends less on intensity than on sincerity.\
You do not need to strain. You do not need to perform certainty. You do not need to ask dramatically.\
You need:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 a settled mind\
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 a clear question\
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 a sincere intention\
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 a willingness to receive what is shown\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Consult the Mo with reverence, simplicity, and honesty.\
Then let the answer speak.\
}